# Protected Route Security

- Classify each route as public, authenticated, anonymous-only, or intentionally unreachable.
- Enforce authentication and authorization on the server at every protected read, mutation, and HTTP boundary.
- Treat layouts, redirects, hidden controls, middleware/proxy checks, and Client Component guards as user experience only.
- Validate and normalize all boundary input before use; authorize the specific resource after identity is known.
- Return the least information needed. Do not reveal resource existence, secrets, internal errors, or authorization policy through unsafe failures.
- Recheck authorization inside Server Actions and Route Handlers even when the invoking page was protected.
- Keep privileged credentials server-only and prevent imports from reaching client bundles.
- Test direct navigation and direct action/endpoint invocation for allowed and denied identities.

Do not invent an authentication provider or role model; follow the downstream project's documented policy.
